From ef35fd11bec1a9d1e90a1730c832ef9d0a1c0c71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaetan Cathelain <gaetan.cathelain@mobile.club>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(display): per-conversation tool_progress override
 (display.platforms.<platform>.tool_progress_conversations)

tool_progress_dm scopes the tool-call narration to DMs, which is one axis
too coarse for a bot that lives in several channels on one platform: the
workshop channel wants the running commentary, every other shared surface
wants silence, and both of them are channels.

Add display.platforms.<platform>.tool_progress_conversations, a chat_id ->
tool_progress mapping applied after the platform setting and after
tool_progress_dm, so the most specific configuration wins:

  display:
    platforms:
      slack:
        tool_progress: off          # channels stay quiet
        tool_progress_dm: all       # DMs narrate
        tool_progress_conversations:
          C0BP2GZUFSR: all          # ...and so does the workshop channel

Cosmetic only. It gates the interim "tool started" bubbles and nothing
else: every conversation resolves the same toolset, the model is offered
the same tool schema (a stable schema is what keeps the prompt cache
warm), tools execute wherever the mention gate let the session through,
and the final answer is delivered everywhere - including the
conversations whose narration is hidden.

It therefore supersedes and reverts the withdrawn platform_tool_conversations
toolset gating (5af9e1e), which read this same policy as a capability
restriction and emptied enabled_toolsets outside the listed conversations,
disarming the agent in any channel a colleague pulled it into. The ask was
display, not capability; this lineage carries the display half only.

Malformed configuration is ignored rather than fail-closed - the opposite
of the withdrawn patch, and deliberately so: a typo in a cosmetic key must
never change what the agent can do, so a non-mapping value or an unlisted
chat id simply leaves the resolved progress_mode alone.

tests/gateway/test_slack_tool_visibility.py drives real gateway turns for
a public channel, the workshop channel and the owner's DM: identical
toolsets everywhere, real tool schemas and a real tool dispatch in the
quiet channel, progress bubbles only where configured, and the final
answer in all three. It also pins the mention gate (configuration only,
no code) against the real SlackAdapter._handle_slack_message.

Amended after an adversarial review of the shipped kit. Slack's adapter
collapses MPIMs into DMs (adapter.py:5512, is_dm = channel_type in
{"im","mpim"} -> chat_type="dm"), so tool_progress_dm: all would have
narrated interim tool calls into group DMs - a shared surface. The deploy
therefore uses a map-only config shape with no tool_progress_dm key at all,
and five tests now pin it: test_group_dm_stays_quiet_without_tool_progress_dm
(a group DM under the map-only shape runs a real tool and stays silent),
test_dm_narrates_via_conversations_map (the owner's 1:1 DM is verbose via its
chat id, not via tool_progress_dm), a parametrized
test_malformed_display_config_never_disarms_the_agent that finally exercises
the previously dead config= hook with a config carrying no display key and one
whose tool_progress_conversations is a string - both complete the turn with a
non-empty toolset, a real tool dispatch and no exception, falling back to
Slack's built-in "off" - and test_bare_off_in_yaml_resolves_to_quiet. That last
one records the measured False-shape semantics: YAML 1.1 parses a bare `off` to
the boolean False, resolve_display_setting passes it through _normalise, whose
`value is False` branch returns the string "off", so _resolved_tp is "off" and
the `_resolved_tp or _env_tp or "all"` chain never sees a falsy value - a bare
`off` is QUIET, identical to the quoted "off". The deploy still writes the
quoted form, because that equivalence rests entirely on that one branch. The
anti-regression guard additionally pins the resolver's signature
(chat_id not in inspect.signature(_get_platform_tools).parameters): capability
cannot become conversation-scoped without changing that line first.

Suite: 25 passed. No production code changed by this amendment.
